# Compatibility

<p class="lede">
ppd {meta.version} is verified on macOS with Paseo {meta.verifiedPaseo}, desktop app and CLI. It relies on parts of
Paseo that are not a public API, and says so when one of them moves instead of blaming your plugin.
</p>

<h2 id="needs">What it needs</h2>

| Tool | For | Without it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Node {meta.node} | everything | |
| Paseo desktop app | the real compiler, evaluator and Lucide list in `ppd check`, the web UI, `agentTimeline` | `ppd check` runs as a labeled approximation; `ppd web` needs a web UI build (`--web-dist`) |
| Paseo CLI | `ppd daemon`, `install`, `dev`, `paseo`, the fake agent | no dev daemon |
| Google Chrome, or Playwright's Chromium | `ppd web`, `PaseoWeb` | no screenshots |
| `react-native` devDependency, or `HERMESC` and `HERMES` | the Hermes compile and VM checks | those two checks skip |
| adb | `ppd android` | no phone |

macOS and Linux. On Linux (CI), there is no Paseo app: daemon tests skip and `ppd check` is an approximation.
Windows is not supported.

<h2 id="relies-on">What ppd relies on</h2>

| Relies on | Used by | When it changes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `compiler.js`, `bundle-evaluator.js` and `manifest.js` from `@getpaseo/server` inside the app's `app.asar` (`dist/server/server/plugins`) | `ppd check` (real compile and server evaluation) | `paseo-compile` fails with "could not load Paseo's plugin compiler", the expected path, and the verified and found versions. `ppd check --approx` or `PASEO_SOURCE` works around it. |
| The Lucide exports in the app's web bundle (`app-dist/_expo/static/js/web/index-*.js`) | icon checks | `lucide-icons` warns and falls back to the plugin's own `lucide-react-native`. |
| `@getpaseo/client` and `ws` inside `app.asar` | `agentTimeline` | the call fails naming the modules it looked for. |
| `paseo daemon run --home`, `PASEO_HOME`, `PASEO_LISTEN` and the `config.json` keys | `ppd daemon up` | a start failure prints the daemon output and how it was started. |
| Accessible names in the web UI ("New workspace", "Open menu", "Workspace actions", "Search commands") | `ppd web`, `PaseoWeb` | a timeout names the label it waited for. |
| Rules vendored from Paseo (client registration, manifest schema, build options) | every `ppd check` (`manifest`, `client-eval`), the client check in `ppd install` and `ppd dev`, and the approximation's compile | drift shows up in the weekly CI job against Paseo main. |

`ppd daemon up` prints a note when the installed Paseo is not {meta.verifiedPaseo}, and `ppd doctor` shows the same text
as a warning on its `paseo CLI` line:

```text
note:  ppd was verified on Paseo <verified>; this is <found>
```

<h2 id="upstream">Tracking Paseo main</h2>

The devkit's CI runs its test suite every week against a fresh build of Paseo main (`PASEO_SOURCE`), and
[`examples/ci.yml`](https://github.com/nkwib/paseo-plugin-devkit/blob/main/examples/ci.yml) does the same for your
plugin. When something breaks, an issue with the message helps:
[nkwib/paseo-plugin-devkit/issues](https://github.com/nkwib/paseo-plugin-devkit/issues).
